Z||000000||Cooter||11-28-2000||10:30 PM||||Is this too big for my 3.4? The smaller unit is from a 88 Turbo Coupe:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dcp01400.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dcp01401.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||afRaceR||11-28-2000||10:41 PM||||It's hard to say without seeing specs on it but it looks alittle big. It may give you too much turbo lag unless you got the boost up pretty high, which you would need to change the pistons to lower compression pistons. <BR>I think I would try to find something kind of in the middle between these two. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||loafer87gt||11-29-2000||12:42 AM||||Kinda off topic, but do you guys remember watching the old Porsches 920's (I'm pretty sure that was the model number) racing. They were crazy, had one HUGE turbo on them, and when it finally spooled up you could see the driver get slammed back in his seat! I always thought they were awesome to watch, and have wished to won a turbo car since||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||11-29-2000||01:43 AM||||I know the tbird turbo will get you a maximum of 17psi.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||11-29-2000||02:24 AM||||Looks like one heck of a christmas present  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wannabe||11-29-2000||09:00 AM||||It's too big, unless you plan to run the 3.4 to 10,000 rpm. That looks like it is off a large diesel engine.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||11-29-2000||09:25 AM||||AAAAAAAAAAGH AS THE ANGELS SING FROM THE HEAVENS and the clouds break to reveal a paper cut out rendering of GOD..<P>DON'T AVERT YOUR EYES! <P>looks like a T-72!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> it'll work.. but may take a while to spool.. if it is a 72 with a super 60 wheel it'll spool (according to the Turbonetics flow charts) at 4000 to full boost on a 3.4 (51lbs of air) and be able to hold it till the motor grenages or your ankle gets tired!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  WHERE did you find that?!?! it retails from turbonetics for $2600!!! <P>and has what looks like a water injection boss on it already!?<P>ok  everyone.. Cooter has just become THE MAN!<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-29-2000).]||||reg||1
